# Pokemon Snap (US) seeds of nielrenned's Pokemon Snap world (v0.8.0). Addresses from the
# world's own fork of the decomp (nielrenned/pokemonsnap, splat.yaml and tools/symbol_addrs.txt)
# and checked against the ROM here: the main segment is ROM 0x1000 at 0x80000400, resident for
# the whole run.
#
# The stub goes over func_80003530 in sys/dma.c, a 1356-byte leaf function (its own 0x430-byte
# frame, no calls out) after dmaReadVPK0. Nothing anywhere in the patched ROM refers to it: no
# jal or j, no lui/addiu or lui/ori pair building its address, no stored word equal to it, across
# every overlay and the world's own segment. tools/count-calls.lua counted 0 calls at four points
# through it over 12,660 frames of play (title, Oak's lab, a course, the photo check and report),
# against a control that ran 12,438 times.
STUB_VRAM=0x80003530
STUB_MAX=1356
# The world's segment and its state block sit at the start of the Expansion Pak, 0x80400000 to
# 0x80405000 (5 pages), and the game itself needs the Pak for them. tools/ram-usage.lua saw nothing
# else touch the Pak in those 12,660 frames: 0x80405000-0x80800000 was zero and never changed. The
# only code in the game that writes the Pak is func_8009B2BC, a RAM test for the Snap Station photo
# printer, which runs only with one attached and would wipe the world's segment too.
AGENT_VRAM=0x80480000
# Past the world's segment, which the patch appends to the 16 MiB image at 0x1000000 (it ends at
# 0x1004360 in v0.8.0).
AGENT_ROM=0x1010000
AGENT_MIN_RAM=0x800000
